{"name":"Amaranth Deep Purple","hex":"#9f2b68","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"amaranth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An imaginary flower that does not wither.","Any of various herbs of the genus Amaranthus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaranth"},{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.","Positioned far from the surface or other reference point, especially down through something or into something."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deep Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Deep Purple are a British rock band formed in London in 1968. They are considered to be among the pioneers of heavy metal and modern hard rock, although their musical style has varied throughout their career. Originally formed as a psychedelic rock and progressive rock band, they shifted to a heavier sound with their 1970 album Deep Purple in Rock. Deep Purple have been referred to as being part of the \"unholy trinity of British hard rock and heavy metal in the early to mid-'70s\", alongside Led Zeppelin and Black Sabbath. Listed in the 1975 Guinness Book of World Records as \"the globe's loudest band\" for a 1972 concert at London's Rainbow Theatre, they have sold over 100 million records worldwide. Deep Purple have also generated several successful spinoff bands, including Rainbow, Whitesnake, and Gillan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Deep_Purple_%281971%29.JPG/330px-Deep_Purple_%281971%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_Purple","wikidata":"Q101505"},{"title":"Amaranth","blocks":[{"text":"Amaranthus is a genus of plants commonly known as amaranths. Some species are known by variants of the common name \"pigweed\". Some members are annual and others are perennial. The plant can grow from 1 to 2.5 metres tall with a succulent, hollow stem. Parts of the plant vary from green to reddish. Catkin-like cymes of densely packed flowers grow in the summer or fall."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Amaranthus_tricolor0.jpg/330px-Amaranthus_tricolor0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amaranth","wikidata":"Q156344"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"},{"title":"Amaranth (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Amaranth is a reddish-rose color that is a representation of the color of the flower of the amaranth plant. The color shown is the color of the red amaranth flower, but there are other varieties of amaranth that have other colors of amaranth flowers; these colors are also shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Amaranthus_tricolor0.jpg/330px-Amaranthus_tricolor0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amaranth_(color)","wikidata":"Q454847"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Deep_Purple_%281971%29.JPG/500px-Deep_Purple_%281971%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Deep_Purple_%281971%29.JPG/500px-Deep_Purple_%281971%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADeep_Purple_(1971).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Deep_Purple_%281968%29.jpg/500px-Deep_Purple_%281968%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Deep_Purple_%281968%29.jpg/500px-Deep_Purple_%281968%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Deep Purple Mark I in 1968. Standing left to right: Nick Simper, Ian Paice, Rod Evans; seated left to right: Ritchie Blackmore, Jon Lord.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADeep_Purple_(1968).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Deep_Purple%2C_Ian_Gillan_1970.jpg/500px-Deep_Purple%2C_Ian_Gillan_1970.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Deep_P